@@ -4055,3 +4055,8 @@
 ## Evidence574 — Checked legal proof feedback and training target binding
 
 Checked legal proof feedback now binds the selected receipt to the current sample, formal obligation, interpretation and dependencies before the trainer accepts the record. The controlled cases cover substituted receipts, changed sources or selected frames, stale interpretations and nested guidance that could redirect a primary update. The published candidate at 4449d6a6 passed all 26 ordinary software cases across 13 functions. Collection, execution and raw JUnit recorded the same cases. Source and resource custody closed. The retained fictional Lean proof is reported separately as input to a private replay. These results leave the production model and statutory admission gates open. [Ordinary26 qualification](/tmp/P7-checked-feedback-revalidated-final-LadvXFyf/actual-Phase7-current-checked-proof-ordinary26-closed.json) · [Code publication](/tmp/P7-checked-feedback-revalidated-final-LadvXFyf/actual-Phase7-ordinary26-check-feedback-three-FF-publication.json)
+
+
+## Evidence575 — Checked Lean translations in legal proof-cache replay
+
+Legal proof-cache replay now requires the translation recorded by the checked Lean receipt to match the canonical request. Matching translations and requests without translations round-trip from disk. The suite rejects a translation present on only one side and a different translation digest. The published implementation at 4cc1311f passed all nine ordinary software cases across five functions. Collection, execution and raw JUnit agreed, and Source and resource custody closed. The tests used fictional proof receipts. [Ordinary qualification](/tmp/P1-proof-cache-translation-current-6btZZr/actual-Phase1-current-cache-translation-ordinary9-closed.json) · [Code publication](/tmp/P1-proof-cache-translation-current-6btZZr/actual-Phase1-cache-translation-ordinary9-three-FF-publication.json)
